message: "If you use this software, please cite it. If you refer to the ideas, please cite the paper (see preferred-citation)."
title: "Shift Intent Left: Intent Contract schema, validator, and reference enforcement point"
abstract: >-
  Reference artifacts for Shift Intent Left (SIL), a lifecycle discipline that
  treats the intent declared for an autonomous coding agent as the earliest
  securable artifact of the SDLC. Includes a JSON Schema for the Intent Contract,
  a validator enforcing four invariants JSON Schema cannot express, and a
  reference enforcement point implementing the admissibility predicate, the
  severity-weighted Intent Drift metric, and a tamper-evident action trace.
